{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Balak son of Zippor.</b> He was one of three people who answered improperly: Cain, Balaam, and Hezekiah. Cain — when the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him, 'Where is Abel your brother?', he answered, 'Am I my brother's keeper?' He should have replied: Master of the Universe, You know everything, and all is revealed before You. Balaam likewise, when He said to him, 'Who are these men?' — he should have replied: You know who they are. Hezekiah, when Isaiah asked him, 'From where did these men come to you?', and he said to him, 'From a far country they came to me, from Babylon' — he should have replied: You are a prophet and you know. And it is difficult for me: why does it not count Adam the First? When the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him, 'Where are you?' — he should have replied: You know, for wisdom had already been placed in him, for at the time he was created he called names [to the animals] and did not sin until the tenth hour. And if you say: remove Hezekiah and insert Adam the First, it works out well — and so it appears, for these three were speaking with the Holy One, blessed be He, but Hezekiah was speaking with the prophet, and the prophets do not know everything."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:58.292826352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}